  "title": "Finishing the London Bills of Mortality: the totals and causes of weekly bills not yet transcribed, 1669 to 1673",
  "done_when": "Every bill has its christened, buried and plague totals and its Aged, Consumption, Convulsion, Dropsie, Feaver and Flox and Small-pox counts agreed by two AIs of different vendors, each read from the photographs of the Wellcome Collection copy in the Death by Numbers image collection, with the dates in the heading copied as evidence.",
